approved_coordinator_effective_core.profile:
Authorize ONE bounded specification-only pass for EC_DURABLE_COMMIT_BINDING_NOT_SELECTED. Using the already selected Snapshot Provenance Profile v1 and EC-SOURCE-STEP-v1, prepare a concrete minimal reviewable contract identifying (1) the persisted object binding exact original E/seed, original event/cut and complete computed P0/P1, (2) append/barrier/commit/expose ordering and (3) incomplete/crash/replay interpretation preserving original physical slots, public vote ordinals, identities and all lineage. Reuse existing selected authority and contracts wherever sufficient. Show exact byte/storage compatibility consequences and required future qualification; do not design a universal storage system or alternative provenance mechanism. This approval authorizes only drafting that contract, not selecting its eventual layout, a new WAL kind, W1 extension or implementation. If a purported already selected immutable binding is supplied, verify exact applicability and evidence instead of treating a hash or assertion as authority. After the specification, publish one exact proposal through Pending decisions and STOP before code/schema/proof/fixture/runtime changes or dependent R2.3 continuation. Preserve all scope17 permissions and restrictions: general R2.3 authority is not being requested again, but does not select the missing storage semantics. No production integration, guard removal, certificate/QC/WAL identity change, new trust, concrete sigma or full R3. R2.3 remains OPEN/Formal NO_GO until its ordinary substantive proof and review gates succeed; named recovery only after that closure. Reject or unresolved edits preserve the current dependent STOP.
Preserve all existing scope17 permissions, restrictions and the previously approved standing R2.3 semantic-delegation authority unchanged.

Extend that standing authority only as follows:

For the remaining isolated feature000 formal/reference R2.3 work, the orchestrator is authorized to design, select, implement, prove and qualify the minimal deterministic persistence/durability/source-association contracts necessary to establish the already approved source/recovery relation, without returning for another human decision merely to select the resulting formal/reference contract.

This specifically includes the current EC_DURABLE_COMMIT_BINDING_NOT_SELECTED boundary.

For EC durability, the orchestrator may, within the isolated formal/reference model:

- define the exact persisted formal/reference object binding original E/seed bytes, original event/cut, and the complete computed P0/P1;
- select exact canonical formal/reference bytes, identifiers, hashes, schema fields/versions and source relations necessary for that binding;
- define append, durability barrier, commit and expose ordering using already approved storage/durability authority and primitives;
- define deterministic incomplete/crash/replay/conflict interpretation;
- preserve and formally bind original physical slots, public vote ordinals, object identities, retries, every retained source occurrence and lineage;
- introduce the minimum isolated formal/reference persistence envelope or record representation needed to express and prove that semantics;
- implement its codecs/checkers/model guards/fixtures/Lean/TLA/refinement machinery and run applicable qualification and two-process reviews;
- revise technical details when proofs or reviews require correction, provided the resulting semantics stay inside this authority envelope.

The orchestrator does not need another Pending decision solely because the resulting proposal chooses among multiple formal/reference byte layouts or representations, provided it selects the minimal deterministic alternative that reuses existing approved authority and does not claim legacy production compatibility.

For this delegated class only, supersede the current instruction requiring STOP after drafting the EC durability proposal. Instead, record the exact selected contract, immutable source inputs, rationale, compatibility consequences and evidence, then continue implementation/proof/composition under the existing sprint unless a boundary below is crossed.

A new Pending decision remains mandatory before any of the following:

- changing deployed legacy production storage semantics or production Init/Next;
- adding or changing a production WAL record kind or production WAL/storage byte encoding;
- claiming that existing legacy histories conform to the new future-generation formal/reference contract without independently established evidence;
- changing existing certificate, QC, signature, WAL or original-object identity;
- introducing a new trust/authority root, factual-history observer or physical-history source of truth;
- weakening or narrowing the approved source/admissible-history domain;
- discarding, synthesizing or relabeling missing/incomplete physical history;
- changing Snapshot Provenance Profile v1, EC-SOURCE-STEP-v1 or another previously selected semantic contract rather than composing the minimum missing binding;
- choosing concrete production deployment values or enabling production integration;
- weakening any Formal GO, compatibility, source-provenance, safety, review or recovery gate;
- entering full R3.

This extension also applies to later R2.3 persistence, durability, provenance, producer/storage-association and history-association gaps of the same class. If they can be resolved by a minimal deterministic isolated formal/reference contract using already approved authority, they are delegated and do not require another human Pending decision.

Every delegated choice must remain explicit, immutable-source-bound and auditable. It must not be hidden as a theorem premise, helper definition, trusted callback, fixture assumption or prevalidated input.

R2.3 remains OPEN until substantive implementation, proof, composition and required reviews actually close it. This delegation is not evidence of correctness, recovery, compatibility or Formal GO. DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines remains downstream of substantive reviewed R2.3 closure, and full R3 remains forbidden.

Retained restrictions:
- No production C++/ABI/Java/sidecar integration, production recovery deployment or arithmetic guard removal; exact compatible merged Formal GO remains required. Future feature000 semantic/model changes are those explicitly selected in this contract, never changes to the deployed legacy generation.
- Preserve existing storage authentication bindings, original signer/object/QC/WAL identities and all retained delivery/source multiplicity. New generation pins/hashes must be qualified; no old-object reinterpretation, migration, relabeling or resigning. No concrete sigma_next.
- F is forbidden. No factual-history observer, new trust/authority root, hidden source-domain restriction, invented source caps, loss/fault erasure, lineage truncation or replacement of missing bytes with successful callbacks. The revised physical-cut claim is explicit, not evidence that the old claim passed.
- Preserve fixed-epoch enrolled Snapshot Provenance Profile v1 authority and deployment boundaries: no unenrolled node, epoch change, trusted-volume compromise/rollback, network bootstrap or universal backup format.
- R1/R2.1/R2.2 stay CLOSED for their original domains. R2.3 stays OPEN until substantive reviewed proof. Named DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines only after reviewed R2.3 closure; full R3 forbidden. No conditional refinement portrayed as production GO.
- No sorry, hidden/circular/public-success axioms, vacuous theorem/domain weakening, opaque accept callbacks or relabeled FAIL/NO_GO. Requalify every affected source/model/refinement/mutant/compatibility/review gate; sequential self-review is not independent attestation.
- No new sprint, reimport, reset, manual graph advancement, fake RESUME/START for STOP, duplicate result/review, nginx-qa patch/deploy/restart, subagents, foreign-file changes or frozen-ref rewrites. Preserve history and healthy demos. ACK removes only scope authorization and never advances graph or bypasses another gate.
- This selection concerns the exact EC-SOURCE-STEP-v1 source interpretation only. It is not approval of a concrete EC durability encoding, runtime producer, new WAL kind, W1 extension, new trust root or physical-history claim. If required composition lacks an independently selected storage/producer rule, expose that residual and STOP rather than assume it.
- This request is specification-only. Approval does not select an EC persisted byte format, extend W1, introduce a WAL kind, authorize implementation/proofs/schemas/fixtures, or waive any gate. Submit the exact resulting proposal and STOP before dependent implementation. No durable=true/source-hash/public-success surrogate.

Existing execution, review and qualification gates remain unchanged. This effective instruction supersedes conflicting historical scope text.

